WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.310
- As the war rages over here in Gaza,

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.040
mediation efforts are being led by Qatar,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.940
a tiny peninsula on the
Persian Gulf 1,100 miles away.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.490
The country has used its
close ties with both Hamas

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.120
and the West to negotiate the
release of hostages from Gaza

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.510
and get others out through the
border crossing with Egypt.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.280
It's just the latest example

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.640
of Qatar's important
role on the world stage,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.920
from helping the US evacuate thousands

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.070
of people from Afghanistan to
brokering a prisoner swap deal

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.843
between the US and Iran.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.100
Here's how Qatar became
such an important player

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.423
in global diplomacy.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.600
Qatar's location and economic clout

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.040
make it strategically important

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.690
to a lot of different countries.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.810
It shares its only land
border with Saudi Arabia,

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.730
a major power in the Middle East,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.580
and it shares the world's
largest natural gas field

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.600
right here with Iran, Saudi's
biggest regional rival.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.480
Exports of liquified natural
gas have made Qatar one

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.370
of the wealthiest countries in the world,

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.950
boosting its influence
in this volatile region.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.590
This has made Qatar a critical
energy partner for a lot

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.840
of countries, especially those in Europe

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.090
because the continent has
been reducing its reliance

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.070
on Russian oil and gas.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.560
Qatar is also important
to the United States,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.990
and right here is the
biggest US military base

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.370
in the Middle East.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.760
It's been a launching pad for
operations in Afghanistan,

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.740
Iraq, and Syria.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.370
Last year, the US made
Qatar a major non-NATO ally.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:29.430
Qatar has also made itself
influential in the broader region

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.540
through Al Jazeera,

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.480
the largest news media
network in the Middle East,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.610
but it has been criticized
in both the Arab world

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.220
and the West for its sometimes
controversial coverage

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.133
of uprisings, wars and other conflicts.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.850
For example, the network
broadcast video messages

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.193
from Osama bin Laden after 9/11.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.000
Nevertheless, Qatar prides
itself on being a meeting place

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.670
for diverse viewpoints,
which was on full display

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.640
when the country hosted
the World Cup last year,

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.640
and its ambassador to the US
recently wrote an opinion piece

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.600
in The Wall Street Journal,

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.410
claiming that "Qatar is the
Mid-East's honest broker."

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:05.940
In the 1980s and '90s

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.790
the country's leaders developed
relationships with Iran,

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:11.309
as well as regional groups like Hamas

00:02:11.309 --> 00:02:13.260
in the Palestinian territories

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.570
and the Muslim Brotherhood in Egypt,

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.760
groups that are considered
terrorist organizations

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.470
in some parts of the world.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:22.170
It also fostered ties
with the Afghan Taliban.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:26.010
In 2013, the Taliban opened
a political office in Qatar

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:29.250
with support from the US
and Afghan governments.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.850
Years of negotiations in
Doha led to a deal in 2020

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.490
for US troops to withdraw
from Afghanistan,

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.193
ending America's longest war.

00:02:37.193 --> 00:02:39.750
(people clapping)

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.450
But the agreement didn't
bring peace to the country.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.030
The Taliban never reached
a power sharing agreement

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.200
with the Afghan government,

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.200
and it seized control of Kabul in 2021.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.410
Qatar helped to evacuate US
citizens in the aftermath,

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.200
and it is now Washington's
diplomatic representative

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.340
in the country.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:00.120
Hamas also opened a political
office in Qatar in 2012

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.520
after a request by the
Obama administration

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.490
to establish indirect
lines of communication,

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.380
and Qatar has provided financial aid

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:11.010
to Palestinians in Gaza,
which is run by Hamas.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.860
That has led to accusations
of funding terrorism,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.440
which Qatar denies.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.570
Qatar's complex web of relationships

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.370
has caused friction with its neighbors.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:24.750
In 2017, it was blockaded
by Saudi Arabia, the UAE,

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.550
Bahrain and Egypt.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.940
They accused Doha of meddling
in their domestic affairs,

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.440
supporting extremist groups,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.260
and being too close to
regional rival Iran.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.420
The four countries
issued a list of demands,

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.310
including shutting down Al Jazeera

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:40.710
and reducing ties with Tehran.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.870
Even though Qatar didn't make concessions,

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.840
the blockade ended in January of 2021,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.750
and the terms of the deal
haven't been made public.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.030
Although the country's
reestablished relations,

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.010
some analysts say that the root causes

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.190
of that diplomatic crisis
haven't been resolved.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:58.440
Today, Qatar's diplomatic relationships

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.090
are in the spotlight once again

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.860
with the country negotiating the release

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:05.583
of hostages taken from
Israel into Gaza by Hamas.

00:04:07.418 --> 00:04:09.210
(bomb exploding)

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.270
But Qatar said that without a
pause in the fighting in Gaza,

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.330
its mediators won't be
able to do their work.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.610
- It's a very, very difficult negotiation

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.740
that we've been dealing with.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.740
I always say that one of
the most difficult mediation

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.330
is difficult between two parties

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.280
that have zero confidence in each other.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.540
- Israeli officials have said

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:30.150
that Qatar's efforts are
crucial at this time,

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:33.183
but so far, only a few
hostages have been released.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.610
And when the crisis is over,

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.230
many of Qatar's partners want it

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.930
to expel Hamas leaders from the country,

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.390
that includes more than
100 members of Congress

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:44.730
who signed a letter to President Biden.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.440
Qatar said that the political office

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.450
of Hamas will remain open as long

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.730
as it can be used toward peace.

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.800
Some diplomats worry
that those Hamas leaders

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.930
could move somewhere
more hostile to the West,

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.000
like Iran or Syria.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.790
That could make any
communication between Hamas,

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.310
Israel and the West even more complicated

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:03.750
in situations like the one

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.450
that is currently unfolding
in the Middle East.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.117
(pensive music)

